  <!-- Headline -->
  <h2>What Actually Makes RedteaGO Different</h2>
  <p>
    RedteaGO's real pitch is the starting price, not a feature list. Its own shop advertises eSIMs from as little as <strong>$0.52</strong> for a Europe-wide (37-country) plan, <strong>$0.70</strong> for a US, Japan, or Thailand plan, and <strong>$2.90</strong> for a global (130+ area) plan, all across a claimed <strong>180+ countries and regions</strong>. Those are entry-level, smallest-data-tier prices rather than what a typical traveler ends up paying, so check the actual GB amount before assuming the headline number is your final one, but even accounting for that, RedteaGO is routinely one of the cheapest per-GB options on this site.
  </p>
  <p>
    We checked RedteaGO's own homepage and FAQ directly and had to correct our own earlier description of it here: this is not a full voice-and-SMS provider by default. See below.
  </p>

  <!-- Codes -->
  <div class="content-box content-box--tan">
