    <ul>
      <li><strong>{{ provider.primaryCode }}</strong>: 5% off all plans (public code, not advertised on RedteaGO's own site)</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top:.75rem;margin-bottom:0;color:#63553F;">If the code does not apply, refresh the cart or try a private window, then retry.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Real operational note instead of generic feature grid / comparison table -->
  <h2>Most Plans Are Data-Only, Not "Complete Communication"</h2>
  <p>
    RedteaGO's own FAQ says plainly that "call and text services are only available in certain regions," and that plans supporting them are marked with a separate "Calls/Texts Available" label rather than being a standard part of every plan. There's also a distinct "Call & Text eSIM" package sold on its own, apart from the regular data plans. If you need a working phone number for calls or texts, don't assume any RedteaGO plan gives you one; check for that label on the specific plan you're buying first.
  </p>
  <p>
    We also couldn't find any unlimited-data plan on RedteaGO's site: everything we saw is sold as a fixed data bucket (2GB, 5GB, and similar), not a flat unlimited allowance. What is confirmed sitewide is hotspot and tethering support, RedteaGO's FAQ states it's available "in all countries and regions," no exceptions by plan type.
  </p>

